<h1>Observing Services Portal</h1>

<p>The Observing Services Portal is useful for applying for ObsTest waiting lists, advanced training, and to apply for ObsCard renewals.</p>

<h2>ObsTest Policy</h2>

<p> ObsTests are regularly held during Michaelmas and Lent Terms on weekends and ocassionally during weekdays or vacations. If you are looking for an ObsTest but have been unable due to scheduling issues, please email the ObsSecs.
Once you have joined the waiting list for the ObsTest and are eligible in accordance with the policy, you will recieve emails to book an ObsTest everytime there are ObsTests held, until you pass your ObsTest. To be removed from this waiting list, please email the ObsSecs.</p>

<h3>Northumberland ObsTest</h3>
<p>To apply for a Northumberland ObsTest, you must be a valid Member of CUAS, and have attended two Northumberland ObsDemos within the current or the previous academic year. 
At the ObsTest, you will have to demonstrate to an ObsSec that you can safely use the Northumberland Telescope on your own. You are highly encouraged to look through the ObsGuide before your test.
If you pass your ObsTest, you will recieve an ObsCard that will allow you to access the Northumberland Telescope.</p>

<h3>Thorrowgood ObsTest</h3>
<p>To apply for a Thorrowgood ObsTest, you must be a valid Member of CUAS, hold an ObsCard (ie. have passed the Northumberland ObsTest) and have attended one Thorrowgood ObsDemo within the current or the previous academic year. 
At the ObsTest, you will have to demonstrate to an ObsSec that you can safely use the Thorrowgood Telescope on your own. You must bring your ObsCard to the ObsTest. You are highly encouraged to look through the ObsGuide before your test.
If you pass your ObsTest, you will recieve a Thorrowgood Access Sticker on your ObsCard.</p>

<h2>Advanced Training Programme Policy</h2>
Advanced Training Programmes can only be held during clear nights, so please excuse the short notice of announcement. Please satisfy yourself that you have a serious interest in the topics before applying.

<h3>Astrophotography Training</h3>
<p>To be eligible for Astrophotography Training, you must be a valid Member of CUAS, hold an ObsCard (ie. have passed the Northumberland ObsTest), and have a serious interest in Astrophotography. For further details about the training, please check out our Astrophotography page. </p>

<h3>Advanced Visual Observing Training</h3>
<p>Advanced Visual Observing Training incorporates guided starhopping using our Dobsonian Telescopes, held only on clear nights. It is an excellent opportunity to get to know and observe with our ObsSecs. 
To be eligible, you must be a valid Member of CUAS, hold an ObsCard (ie. have passed the Northumberland ObsTest), and have a serious interest in Visual Observing. </p>

